kind: profile
question: do shared BF16 tensor-core HC prompt products reduce 4K prefill latency on GB10?
term: prefill tokens per second for one 4096-id code-fn request per arm
unit: %
predict: +10..+30
condition: load the baseline and candidate once each on an otherwise idle GPU
  in one lease. Use identical NVFP4 stored weights, prompt ids, C=1, draft off,
  and two generated tokens. Use separate build targets and check distinct
  binary hashes before loading. Restore the host clock cap on every exit.
decide-in: report the observed ratio and actual one-request sample counts.
decide-below: inspect remaining BF16 MMA throughput before another candidate.
decide-above: check input length, cache hits and binary provenance.
